OL,3,AHow much could Trump's 'economic D-Day'
OL,4,Ahurt Iran?
OL,5,
OL,6,FNearly six months after US President
OL,7,FDonald Trump vowed a swift victory over
OL,8,FIran, the conflict appears to be at a
OL,9,Fstandstill, with prospects of a
OL,10,Fmilitary victory or negotiated
OL,11,Fsettlement growing dimmer.
OL,13,FTo break the deadlock, Trump has vowed
OL,14,Fan "economic D-Day" under which any
OL,15,Fcountry that does business with Iran
OL,16,Fwould face "tremendous" economic
OL,17,Fconsequences.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11910
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1787293541
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws           G10/40
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AHow much could Trump's 'economic D-Day'
OL,4,Ahurt Iran?
OL,5,
OL,6,FIran, however, has long faced sanctions
OL,7,Fand has so far shown a willingness to
OL,8,Fendure pain, and a capacity to adapt to
OL,9,Fimmense economic and military pressure
OL,10,Fas the conflict drags on.
OL,12,FThe key question for the US then
OL,13,Fbecomes, will further sanctions work
OL,14,Fwhere other strategies have failed?
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
